WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.734
During this week's

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.901
battle on the House floor

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.837
over the nust-pass defense spending bill,

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.372
there was an amendment to prohibit

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.239
the Defense Department

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.441
from requiring diversity training.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.310
The amendment offered by Arizona

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.611
Republican Congressman

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.279
Eli Crane, was under debate

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.315
when this happened.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.217
My amendment has nothing to do

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.284
with whether or not colored

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.652
people or black people

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.188
or anybody can serve.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.190
It has nothing to do with, Mr.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.158
Speaker,

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.227
any of that stuff.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.862
I'd like to be recognized

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.631
to have the words colored people stricken

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:33.533
from the record.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.802
I find it offensive

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.371
and very inappropriate.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.440
That rebuke came from Ohio Congresswoman

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.775
Joyce Beatty.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.243
And then Crater Crane,

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.078
we should say, later apologized

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.079
and offered this

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.180
when he said

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.148
in a heated floor

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.215
debate on my amendment

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:49.883
that would prohibit

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.118
discrimination on the color of one's skin

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.820
in the armed forces.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.554
I misspoke.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.889
Every one of us is made

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.158
in the image of God and created equal

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.794
Quote from the congressman there.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:01.428
Joining us now

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.796
with more on this to Nevada

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.464
Congressman Steve Horsford,

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.665
a Democrat and chair

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.867
of the Congressional Black Caucus.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:08.701
Congressman, thanks

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.869
so much for being with us.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:10.703
What did you make?

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.304
I mean,

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:13.740
first, the congressman from Arizona

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.543
making that remark on the House floor

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:17.510
during this

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.112
debate over the defense

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.915
authorization bill, appropriation bill,

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.384
and then his apology afterwards.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.319
What did you make of all of that?

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:27.954
What's going on

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.826
Well, Jim, thank you for having me on.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.494
I'm here in Orlando, Florida,

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.995
at a democracy for the people

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:36.763
I've been

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.465
talking to, constituents

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:39.399
with the Congressional Black

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.867
Caucus Institute

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.235
about the issues that matter,

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.170
from voting rights

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.606
to the courts, to our schools.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.075
But what that member

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.610
did, Representative Crane from

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.846
Arizona, was unbecoming.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.247
It was unprofessional.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.116
It was insensitive.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:02:00.286
The word itself has vestiges of racism.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.021
For that word

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:05.191
to be used on the House floor in 20, 23

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:08.027
is unconscionable.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.563
While he may have publicly acknowledged

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.801
his error, he still has not

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.603
personally apologized

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:17.871
to the member,

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.272
Representative Joyce Beatty,

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:22.075
that it was directed towards or the body.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.710
And look,

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.478
Representative Crane and people

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.112
like Senator

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.147
Tuberville

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.916
have proven time and time again

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:32.652
why the importance of diversity, equity

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.420
and inclusion training

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.523
is actually needed in this moment

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.457
as Secretary

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.191
Lloyd Austin

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.560
said of the Department of Defense.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.462
Our diversity is our strength.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.998
We have over 40% of our service members

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.567
who are individuals of color.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:51.404
And so to have this resource within

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:52.071
the Pentagon

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.106
is something

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.508
that is important to our service members.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.012
And important to our national security.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:00.647
And it's unfortunate

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.148
that the extreme faction

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.384
of the Republican Congress

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.519
chose to use this as a wedge issue.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.722
Against our military.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:10.557
And I mean,

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:12.258
do you accept the congressman's apology

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:16.729
Well, he hasn't

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:17.197
given that

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.998
apology directly to the body

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.334
or to the member that it was targeted to.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.936
But the larger point is it's

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.305
not about any one individual.

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:28.508
It's about the vestiges of why

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:33.179
they are using woke as a wedge issue.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:35.682
Look, if you if you're against

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:37.183
people of color

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.285
being in the military, just say it.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.120
If you're against us

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.156
having representation

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:45.491
in the private sector, just say it.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:49.629
But it's time out for using these issues

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:50.964
to divide us

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.765
rather than to bring us together

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:53.900
as a nation.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.068
Well, and you mentioned

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.169
Republican Senator Tommy

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.537
Tuberville of Alabama

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:58.605
and what he was saying

00:03:58.605 --> 00:03:59.505
earlier on in the week

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.641
when he was defending the use of the term

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:02.242
white

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.076
nationalism and

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:03.743
I was talking to one

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.445
of your Democratic colleagues

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:06.479
in the previous hour,

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:07.447
and I was asking her

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.215
and I'll ask you the same question,

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.450
whether or not

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.452
these these two episodes

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.286
highlight some of the

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:13.753
that perhaps

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.655
the American people aren't aware of,

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:16.055
that there are

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.257
these kinds of attitudes

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.525
floating around up on Capitol Hill, more

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.593
so than we realize.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.728
What's your sense of that?

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.299
Senator Tuberville

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.701
is using a Jim Crow

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.771
era tradition of the Senate,

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:33.840
which is a blue slip to

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.377
to uphold the confirmation of hundreds,

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.480
hundreds of military nominees

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.782
who are essential

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.684
to our national security.

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.919
These are highly qualified people.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:47.987
These are people who should be

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:48.788
in their position.

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:51.824
It's the first time in 164 years

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.393
that the Marine Corps

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:55.795
has not had a commandant confirmed

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:56.929
by the Senate.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.965
We currently have an acting person

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.967
in that role.

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:01.934
Unfortunately,

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.336
this is why the Congressional Black

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:06.606
Caucus had to call on Chairman Durbin

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.809
to reform the blue slip process,

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.411
not only for the military,

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.413
but for federal judges

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.682
and other important positions, because

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.584
it's it's past time.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.353
It's long past time

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.455
for these types of traditions.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:25.425
Which have a history in segregation

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.759
and Jim Crow

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:27.560
to still be

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.227
used in

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.563
the United States Senate in 20, 23.

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:33.633
We've called for that to be to end

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.902
or to be drastically reformed.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:37.804
And we're hoping

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:40.073
that Chairman Durbin will take us up

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:42.041
on that that request

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:44.010
and this defense bill has been described

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.278
as dead on arrival in the Senate.

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:46.879
But it goes to the Senate where Democrats

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:48.448
are expected to strip out

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:49.615
these HOT-Button issues

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:50.950
that were attached to it.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.252
And still has to go back to the House.

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:54.787
And I guess I'm curious

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.356
if some of those provisions

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:58.424
somehow are left in the legislation

00:05:58.424 --> 00:05:59.192
coming out of the Senate,

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.493
coming back to the House.

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:01.361
Is there any chance

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:02.495
that you would vote for that other

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:03.730
do you think

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.498
the vast majority of Democrats

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:06.399
would have any hope

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.735
of supporting that piece of legislation?

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:11.204
Or might we end up in a situation

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.972
where this defense spending

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:14.107
bill is really

00:06:14.107 --> 00:06:15.508
just held up for months on end

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:17.577
because of these kinds of attachments,

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:18.511
these kinds of amendments

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:19.345
that have been added to it?

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:22.849
Yeah.
Not only

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.984
are they trying to defund

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:26.853
diversity, equity and inclusion,

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:29.522
but they're denying service members

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:32.925
access to reproductive justice, service

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.527
members who do not have a choice

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:36.062
in where they're deployed.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.530
And if they happen to be deployed

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.531
to a state

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:39.332
like Florida,

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:40.366
where I am at today

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:43.436
with Representative Maxwell or Texas,

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:43.836
where they're

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:46.472
now trying to take these rights away.

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:48.875
Those servicemembers don't have a choice.

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:49.909
So, yes,

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:50.643
the Senate

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:52.478
does have to act to correct

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.781
these most extreme provisions

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:56.382
that now have been advanced.

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:57.283
It's unfortunate

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:57.884
that Speaker

00:06:57.884 --> 00:07:01.154
McCarthy allowed the far right faction

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:02.588
to take over this bill.

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.490
This is the first time, Jim,

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:05.825
that I've not been able

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:07.326
to vote for the National Defense

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.594
Authorization Act.

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:10.863
I have
for military installations

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.031
in my district in Nevada.

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:14.400
I support providing

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.335
funding to our military and

00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:19.172
their ability to have the resource

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:20.106
as an the tools,

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.908
but not when it includes

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:23.476
these wedge issues

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:24.777
that are against people's

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:27.013
fundamental right to health care,

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:28.981
reproductive justice,

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:32.485
or that defund and erode

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.755
diversity and equity, which is a strength

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:38.224
within our military, not a weakness

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:39.926
And I want to get your thoughts on

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:40.593
some new reporting

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:41.761
that we have over here at CNN,

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:43.563
that secretaries of state in Pennsylvania

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:45.798
and New Mexico have testified

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:46.933
to that special counsel,

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:49.001
a grand jury investigating

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:51.704
Trump's actions after the 2020 election.

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:53.105
What did you make of that?

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.475
I know Nevada was another state

00:07:55.475 --> 00:07:57.310
that had the issue

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.312
of fraudulently lectures,

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:00.246
phony electors

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:01.814
being advanced to try to overturn

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.082
the election results.

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:04.250
That was something that you encountered

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:04.917
in your state.

00:08:06.052 --> 00:08:06.752
I guess

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.488
what is your sense of how this

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.122
this investigation

00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:11.257
is proceeding over there

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:13.192
at the Justice Department?

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.029
Well, I want to commend

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:18.631
the attorney general

00:08:18.631 --> 00:08:20.533
and the special prosecutor

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:22.435
for doing their job.

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.070
But this is why we're here.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:24.937
In Orlando,

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:27.173
having a forum with constituents

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:30.009
to talk about the attacks on democracy.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:31.744
This is not only about

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:33.279
the former president

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:35.815
and those who were involved in

00:08:36.482 --> 00:08:39.585
overturning a duly elected election

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:42.221
or to deny the voters

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:44.357
the results of that election.

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:45.892
By over by Biden,

00:08:45.892 --> 00:08:49.128
by not upholding the electoral process.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:51.764
You know,
I was there on January 6th

00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:53.032
at the US Capitol.

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:54.000
It was not just

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.701
an attack on our building.

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:58.471
It was an attack on the foundations

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:01.340
of our democracy, which are our schools.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:02.441
It's the courts.

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:04.076
And it's the most important

00:09:04.076 --> 00:09:05.378
and most fundamental right,

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:06.812
which is our right to vote.

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:07.313
That's why

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:08.681
the Congressional Black Caucus,

00:09:08.681 --> 00:09:09.582
our members

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:12.485
are working to pass the voting.

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:15.421
John Lewis Voting Rights Enhancement Act.

00:09:15.655 --> 00:09:17.823
It's the first time in 40 years

00:09:17.823 --> 00:09:19.892
that Republicans have not worked with us

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:21.427
to reauthorize that.

00:09:21.427 --> 00:09:22.762
These are the cornerstones

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:24.063
of our democracy.

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:24.764
We'll be talking

00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:26.699
to constituents here later

00:09:26.699 --> 00:09:27.600
about what

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.669
they have, their role

00:09:29.669 --> 00:09:30.403
and their power

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:31.771
in ensuring that we continue

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:33.639
to uphold our democracy.

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:34.574
At a time

00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:35.575
that it's under attack,

00:09:35.575 --> 00:09:37.643
not just the last election,

00:09:37.643 --> 00:09:40.012
but the elections to come.

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:41.647
All right, Congressman Steve Horsford,

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:42.748
thanks very much for your time.

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:43.316
We appreciate it.

00:09:46.085 --> 00:09:47.219
Thank you for having me.

